  "lineage": "Los Angeles classic hip-hop tradition emerging in late-1980s through Ice-T, N.W.A, and the broader Compton-and-South-Central LA gangsta-rap movement. Characterized by funk-and-P-funk-derived synthesizer-heavy production (especially in 1990s G-funk era), confrontational street-life narrative content, and slower mid-tempo grooves than East Coast. Dr. Dre's The Chronic (1992) and Snoop Doggy Dogg's Doggystyle (1993) consolidated the canonical G-funk sound.",
